From: Fursoy CPU Team <fursoy@fursoy.org>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: cpufeature: Report misaligned access as unsupported for trap-only hardware

Fursoy Slice-0 handles misaligned memory accesses via hardware exception trap
without hardware misaligned support. Set misaligned_access_speed to
RISCV_HWPROBE_MISALIGNED_UNSUPPORTED to avoid slow boot probe cycles and
truthfully report baseline hardware capabilities.

---
 arch/riscv/kernel/cpufeature.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/riscv/kernel/cpufeature.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/kernel/cpufeature.c
@@ -585,6 +585,10 @@ static void check_unaligned_access(int cpu)
 	void *src;
 	long speed = RISCV_HWPROBE_MISALIGNED_SLOW;
 
+	/* Hardware does not support misaligned accesses without trap */
+	per_cpu(misaligned_access_speed, cpu) = RISCV_HWPROBE_MISALIGNED_UNSUPPORTED;
+	return;
+
 	/* We are already set since the last check */
 	if (per_cpu(misaligned_access_speed, cpu) != RISCV_HWPROBE_MISALIGNED_UNKNOWN)
 		return;
